[17592186275172 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275172 #edb/ref 1071 "A bag contains blue and green buttons. The ratio of blue buttons to the total number of buttons is $2:7.$ If there are $14$ blue buttons,  how many green buttons are in the bag?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275172 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d66fb6cc-b6c6-55ab-abc9-f32c6026bbc2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275172 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given that the ratio of blue buttons to the total number of buttons is $\\frac{2}{7}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of blue buttons, and the denominator represents the total number of buttons.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $14$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 7}{7\\times 7}=\\frac{14}{49}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are a total of $49$ buttons in the bag. \nSo, the number of green buttons is\n\n$$\n49-14=35.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429225 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429225 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 3746->563. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429225 #edb/ref 1036 #edb/ref 17592186050174 #edb/